title: Wheel Pottery
---
completion_date: 2024-12-17
---
craft_type: pottery
---
body:

My friend is really into pottery and invited me to join for a class at a local workshop. Since I'd never done pottery before and I had wanted to try it for a while, I said yes! It was a six week course in November/December 2024, and a group of five friends and friends-of-friends went together.

Mostly what I learned was that pottery isn't for me. I don't like having my hands covered in mud for a couple hours, don't have much need for pottery items, and prefer hobbies I can easily pick up and put down at home. I also struggled with the teaching style of the class, especially the instructors doing the changes for me instead of answering my questions so I could do it myself and the lack of an overview to understand what would happen next. My friends had done this before and could answer a lot of questions which was super helpful but not enough to get me hooked.

I thought I would like the two spiral dishes the best, but ended up liking the chunky little mug that was the first thing I made the best. It makes a great snack holder at my desk.

---
summary: I tried pottery and learned I don't like it, but at least I got a nice mug.
